  "doc.title": "How Can a Bet on the Future Have a Fair Price? · A Hands-on Essay",
  "doc.desc": "Nobody knows next year's share price, yet options on it trade thousands of times a day at nearly the same price. This essay starts from \"a forward price is not a forecast\" and climbs through the binomial tree, geometric Brownian motion, the Black–Scholes formula and its partial differential equation, the Greeks and hedging, then shows where it fails: the volatility smile, fat tails, margin and clearing, and the state of the market in November 2026. Thirteen hands-on models. Mathematics and market structure only; not investment advice.",
